00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:00,920
Same man,

00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:02,220
same room,

00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,880
same tired eyes at the end of a long day.

00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,360
Tonight, he makes one small choice,

00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:12,620
and that choice splits his life in two.

00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,500
In one life, he picks up his phone.

00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,060
In the other, he picks up a book.

00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:21,480
One year from now, these two men won't

00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:22,480
recognize each other.

00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,220
The phone feels good,

00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:26,420
instantly.

00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,660
A video, a laugh, another one.

00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:33,300
His shoulders drop. His brain gets a small

00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,420
reward and asks for one more.

00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,020
The book does not feel good. He reads the

00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,740
same line three times.

00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:42,920
His eyes drift to the clock.

00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:46,920
Ten pages feel like a hundred. "Just five

00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,720
more minutes," says the scroller.

00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,560
It's 2:00 in the morning.

00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,880
The reader closes the book after 10 pages,

00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,140
frustrated.

00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,880
And honestly, on night one, the phone is

00:00:58,920 --> 00:00:59,280
winning.

00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:02,200
One of them is relaxed, the other is

00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:02,580
bored.

00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:05,160
That's why most people choose the phone.

00:01:05,640 --> 00:01:08,280
The reward comes first, the bill comes

00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:08,620
later.

00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:12,020
Night two, he almost doesn't open it.

00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,420
Night three, he reads on the bus, mostly

00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:16,360
to prove he can.

00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:18,100
Day five,

00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,740
the phone is the first thing he touches in

00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,860
the morning and the last thing he sees at

00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:23,180
night.

00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:26,060
Breakfast with a screen, bathroom with a

00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,880
screen, bed with a screen.

00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,820
The days start to blur.

00:01:30,860 --> 00:01:34,120
Day five, same chair, same cup of tea,

00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:37,540
same 10 pages. Not because he wants to,

00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,240
because he decided to.

00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:42,280
It still isn't fun, but it's becoming a

00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:42,760
pattern.

00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:44,800
Day 21,

00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:48,440
something feels off. He's tired, even

00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,220
after sleeping.

00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:52,280
Small things annoy him. He snaps at his

00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,380
mother over nothing.

00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:56,840
Then he feels low and reaches for the one

00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,200
thing that makes him feel better,

00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:01,200
the phone, the same thing that's making

00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,160
him feel worse.

00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,980
Day 21, something changes. He looks up,

00:02:07,260 --> 00:02:09,539
and he's read 20 pages without noticing.

00:02:10,139 --> 00:02:12,340
The words don't fight him anymore. He

00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:13,640
falls asleep easier.

00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,180
The hard part is getting easier.

00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,260
Then the book starts leaking into his

00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:22,020
life. He chooses his words more carefully

00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:25,200
at work. He thinks before he reacts. He

00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,340
wakes up a little earlier because he wants

00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:28,760
to know what happens next.

00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,860
One habit is quietly changing the others.

00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:33,560
Day 90,

00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:36,720
look at them now. The scroller's days are

00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,900
copies of each other. Same bed, same glow,

00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:41,100
same results.

00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:44,140
The reader's days look the same too, but

00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,860
he doesn't. A stack of finished books,

00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:49,700
notes on the wall, a calmer face.

00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:53,140
Ninety days ago, the phone felt easy and

00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,260
the book felt hard.

00:02:54,860 --> 00:02:56,860
Now, it's the other way around.

00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,640
Month six,

00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:01,140
an old friend invites them both out for

00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,680
dinner. The scroller says yes, then

00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,100
cancels an hour before.

00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:09,220
Bed feels easier. The reader goes. He asks

00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,540
questions. He actually listens. Two

00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:14,320
hours feel like 20 minutes.

00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,160
Meanwhile, the scroller watches the dinner

00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,860
photos appear on his feed. He double-taps

00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:20,200
one,

00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:21,940
then keeps scrolling.

00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,140
He knows something is wrong, so he

00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:29,520
searches, "How to fix your life." A video

00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,820
about discipline, then one about

00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:34,680
productivity, then one about waking up at

00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:35,220
5:00 a.m.

00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,020
Forty minutes later, he's still in bed,

00:03:38,620 --> 00:03:41,720
still scrolling. He learned everything. He

00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,780
changed nothing.

00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:45,600
Month 11,

00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:48,780
the manager calls him in. A new role has

00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,120
opened, one that needs someone who thinks

00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:54,040
clearly, writes well, and stays calm under

00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:56,760
pressure. Nobody saw the 10 pages a

00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:59,700
night. They only see the result, but he

00:03:59,760 --> 00:04:00,900
knows where it came from.

00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:04,540
Day 365,

00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:08,980
same room, same night, same man. A year of

00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,940
pages became more than 20 books. A

00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,280
year of five more minutes became more than

00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:17,079
a thousand hours on a screen. Neither of

00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:20,019
them changed in one day. They changed one

00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:21,040
night at a time.

00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:25,740
That night, for the first time, he sees

00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:29,360
the other life, the new job, the smile, a

00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,300
man with his face. He looks at his phone,

00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,180
and for the first time, he turns it face

00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:38,380
down. He opens a book. He reads the same

00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:41,420
line three times, exactly like the other

00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:42,880
one did on night one.

00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:45,960
The phone gives you a good night. The book

00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:49,080
gives you a good life. Tonight, which one

00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:49,880
will you pick up?
